NV_PK(59,{"the central mountain range is the backbone of taiwan it runs about 340 kilometers from north to south":"","the xueshan range is in the northwest its highest peak is xueshan":"","the yushan range holds taiwan's highest peak yushan":"","the alishan range is the lowest of the five ranges and the closest to the plains":"","the coastal range is on the east coast it sits on the philippine sea plate":"","jade mountain is 3 952 meters high it is the highest peak in northeast asia":"","xueshan is taiwan's second highest peak at 3 886 meters":"","the chianan plain is taiwan's largest plain tainan sits on it":"","the pingtung plain is taiwan's second largest plain":"","the yilan plain is a river delta in the northeast it gets lots of rain":"","the taipei basin is a low bowl ringed by hills about 2 6 million people live here":"","the east rift valley lies between the central range and the coastal range":"","the taiwan strait is only 126 kilometers wide at its narrowest":"","the penghu islands are about ninety basalt islands in the taiwan strait":"","kenting is at taiwan's southern tip with coral reefs and warm beaches":""});